<file path="prompts/concerns/v1.yml">
version: concerns-v1
purpose: |
  Extract the two most pressing concerns that OnRecord editors should highlight in the recap notes so staff can confirm them with the transcript or subject matter experts.
input_schema:
  transcript: |
    Full cleaned transcript text for a session. Expect speaker tags, sanitization, and an emphasis on action or risk statements.
output_schema:
  key_concerns: |
    Exactly two entries. Each should include a concise title, a detailed description, and optional evidence spans or labels that tie the concern to a transcript fragment.
examples:
  - input:
      transcript: |
        Reporter: Will downtown resiliency funding impact the emergency shelter budget? City Planner: The fund shifts 20% of the resiliency allocation to shelters, but only after pilot studies.
    output:
      key_concerns:
        - title: Funding shift
          detail: 20% of the resiliency budget will be redirected to the shelter program contingent on upcoming pilot results.
        - title: Implementation caveat
          detail: The reallocation fully depends on a pilot study, so the shelter funding is not guaranteed beyond the trial.
</file>

<file path="prompts/followups/v1.yml">
version: followups-v1
purpose: |
  Surface follow-up questions that reporters or staff should ask after the session in order to clarify outstanding facts, status, or next steps.
input_schema:
  transcript: |
    Approved transcript text. Questions should probe points of ambiguity or action items.
output_schema:
  follow_up_questions: |
    Array of 1-3 question-formatted sentences. Each question must end with a question mark and relate directly to the transcript.
examples:
  - input:
      transcript: |
        Moderator: Please confirm the new timeline. Staff: We are still waiting on the consultant for final dates, but hope to complete by April.
    output:
      follow_up_questions:
        - When will the consultant share the final timeline, and who will approve it?
        - Should we expect any interim updates before the April target?
</file>

<file path="prompts/recap/v1.yml">
version: recap-v1
purpose: |
  Produce the authoritative OnRecord recap for a pressroom transcript: summarize the session, call out the two most important concerns, list follow-up questions, and remind editors that the recap is a draft (no medical advice or directives).
input_schema:
  transcript: |
    Cleaned transcript text (string, typically 2k-20k characters) pulled from Supabase. The transcript may already include speaker labels and sanitized content (no PII or classified detail).
output_schema:
  summary: |
    String containing approximately three concise sentences (80-400 characters) that highlight the main takeaways and tone of the session.
  key_concerns: |
    Array of exactly two objects (title, detail) that surface a key takeaway and a supporting detail. Optional evidence_span and label fields describe where the concern came from.
  follow_up_questions: |
    Array of question-formatted strings (each ending with a question mark) offering at least one action item or verification request.
  safety_notes: |
    Safety-focused sentence that explicitly labels the recap as a draft and refrains from offering medical or legal directives.
  verification_notes: |
    Optional sentence describing how staff should confirm statements before publishing.
examples:
  - input:
      transcript: |
        Moderator: We are here to review the climate resilience plan. Councilmember: We will release new dashboards by March that track stormwater permits. Engineer: The downtown transit working group will share ridership data every Friday.
    output:
      summary: |
        The council committed to delivering a new climate resilience dashboard, promised weekly transit stats, and framed the recap as a draft that needs confirmation before sharing.
      key_concerns:
        - title: Key takeaway
          detail: Council leadership pledged a March dashboard rollout for stormwater permit tracking.
          evidence_span:
            start_offset: 35
            end_offset: 104
        - title: Conversation detail
          detail: Downtown transit will add a Friday cadence of ridership statistics to support decision-making.
      follow_up_questions:
        - What metrics will the dashboard publish first?
      safety_notes: Draft recap only; verify all facts with the transcript and treat the content as informational, not medical advice.
      verification_notes: Compare every highlighted claim against the audio transcript before publishing.
</file>

